:Tufelli_masonry_typeD a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Tufelli_masonry_typeD"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "ENTIRELY assumed, not observed: scored identically to typeB (the 'ordinary/irregular' type) as the most defensible default for an unexceptional rendered facade in the same aggregate, rather than typeA (visibly higher quality, tied to specific observed stonework at door openings that this facade's render gives no evidence for) or typeC (visibly patched/reworked, again no evidence either way). This is the weakest-grounded of the four classifications - revisit first if render is ever removed, or if there is independent reason (archival, structural survey) to place this facade in a specific construction phase."@en ;
    skos:definition "Fully rendered facade, masonry not directly observable - assumed by construction-era analogy to typeB"@en ;
    skos:note "A-417/417_b (WhatsApp Image 2023-06-01 at 14.51.52/53) and A-420/a420 (WhatsApp Image 2023-06-01 at 14.50.52-55): fully plastered in every available survey photo, no exposed masonry"@en .

:Tufelli_masonry_typeB a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Tufelli_masonry_typeB"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Same conservative mortar assumption as typeA (plain lime, not hydraulic-boosted)"@en,
        "Vertical joint staggering scored 'partially_staggered' from the visibly less regular coursing - not measured"@en ;
    skos:definition "Irregular tufo masonry, discontinuous coursing, brick relieving arches at openings, squared corner quoins"@en ;
    skos:note "A-417/417_c (corner building, Vicolo del Cabalino - WhatsApp Image 2023-06-01 at 14.50.40/41/42/43) and A-418/418-a (WhatsApp Image 2023-06-01 at 14.50.47/48, brick arch over a round-headed window): irregular unit sizes, less continuous coursing than typeA"@en .

:Tufelli_masonry_typeA a owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Tufelli_masonry_typeA"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Mortar scored plain 'lime' (conservative) rather than crediting the pozzolana content mentioned in the manuscript with a hydraulic-lime-level score - the pozzolana's real contribution to mortar performance was not tested, only described qualitatively"@en,
        "Vertical joint staggering scored 'partially_staggered' (conservative) rather than 'properly_staggered' - not directly measurable from the available photos at typical phone-camera resolution/angle"@en ;
    skos:definition "Regular tufo masonry, fairly continuous coursing, well-cut stone voussoirs at openings"@en ;
    skos:note "A-419/a419 photos (WhatsApp Image 2023-06-01 at 14.50.49/50/51): stone arch over a door with well-dressed voussoirs, courses fairly regular though not perfectly continuous"@en .

